  "id": "Compound::DB01185 - Gene::367",
  "verbalization": "Fluoxymesterone, an anabolic steroid, is linked to Ar through a shared pathway involving Oxandrolone, an anabolic agent. Both Fluoxymesterone and Oxandrolone are classified as 3-oxo steroids, and they both bind to Ar, suggesting a common mechanism of action. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Fluoxymesterone causes various effects, including Androgenetic Alopecia, Enlarged Clitoris, and Peliosis Hepatis, all of which are mediated by Oxandrolone. This suggests a broader role for 3-oxo steroids in modulating Ar activity, possibly through shared receptor binding or downstream signaling pathways. The integration of these paths highlights a potential dependency on 3-oxo steroids for Ar interaction, reinforcing the notion that Fluoxymesterone and Oxandrolone may share a functional relationship through their interaction with Ar. The evidence supports a mechanism where 3-oxo steroids, through their binding to Ar, influence physiological outcomes, with Fluoxymesterone and Oxandrolone acting as potential activators of this pathway.",
